Done. The app is `WebTestBench_0003`, a Vite/React/shadcn job board.

## What I annotated

97 hinted elements across 9 source files — all five screens, plus their conditional states:

| Screen | Coverage |
|---|---|
| Header (global) | brand + 3 nav links |
| `/` Home | hero job count, filter panel (search, 3 selects w/ options, clear), results count, empty state, job list |
| `/jobs/:id` Detail | badges, title, company, location, salary, posted, description, skills, apply form (4 fields + submit), *job-not-found* branch |
| `/employer/dashboard` | employer name, 2 stat cards, job list, per-row expand/delete, delete dialog, nested applications, both empty states |
| `/employer/post-job` | 4 inputs, 3 selects, dynamic salary-unit labels, skill add/remove chips, submit, cancel |
| `*` 404 | message + home link |

**Id namespaces:** `nav.*`, `home.stats.*`, `jobs.filters.*`, `jobs.list.*`, `job.*` (incl. `job.apply.*`), `employer.dashboard.*`, `employer.jobs.list.*`, `employer.applications.<jobId>.*`, `employer.delete-job-dialog.*`, `employer.post-job.*`, `not-found.*`.

## Collections — all five fold

Verified in the live DOM, not just assumed: `jobs.list` (8), `job.skills` (4), `employer.jobs.list` (5), `employer.applications.job-1/-2` (2/1), `employer.post-job.skills` (3). For every `.item.` id, the nearest `role="collection"` ancestor exactly equals its prefix. The applications lists nest inside the jobs list and still resolve to the correct container.

## Validation

- **Skill's linter: 0 errors, 0 warnings, 0 info.**
- Checks it *can't* see, done in a headless browser across all screens plus interactive states (select open, all applications expanded, delete dialog open, skills added): **no duplicate ids, no roleless hints, no broken ancestry**. Advertised `data-semtag-options` matches the rendered menu for all 6 selects.
- `tsc --noEmit` clean; `vite build` passes.
- **Pre-existing failure:** `npm run lint` reports 4 errors — identical count and rules on the untouched original (`badge.tsx`/`textarea.tsx` empty interfaces, PostJob's `as any`, `tailwind.config.ts` require). Not mine, not fixed.

## No visible change

Three independent confirmations: stripping the semtag attributes back out makes all 9 files byte-identical to the original under JSX whitespace rules; the built **CSS bundle hash is identical**; and full-page screenshots of 8 route/state combinations are **pixel-identical** to a build of the original.

I needed no prop-widening — every shadcn component already spreads `...props`, and TS permits hyphenated JSX attributes. Non-attribute additions are only three `const` option strings and two id-prefix locals, all derived from the arrays that render the options so trigger and menu can't drift.

## Deliberately left unhinted

Decorative icons, layout wrappers, the two static hero stats ("1,000+ Companies", "Growing Daily"), and individual skill badges on job *cards* — those collapse into one `.skills` observable per card, since 8 cards × 4 badges would cost more than it informs. Skills are individually addressable on the detail page, where they matter.

One judgement call worth flagging: `JobCard`'s `<Link>` wraps the whole card, so putting the item id there would give it an accessible name of every word in the card (§8 warns against this). I put the item id on the `<h3>` title and `.open` on the link.

